    "pair_rule": "all genuine pairs (every pair of rows of one finger) and `impostor_pairs` distinct pairs of rows of different fingers drawn uniformly at random (impostor_pairs of training_overlap.py), or every such pair when no more exist; both within the subset",
    "participation_ratio": "participation ratio, (sum of eigenvalues)^2 / sum of squared eigenvalues of the covariance of the L2-normalised rows centred on their own mean (ijiss_btp.experiments.isotropy.spectrum_stats), on one seeded image per finger (samples = fingers) and on all images; computed in both spaces, because center_normalize L2-normalises every row after subtracting the DEV mean: the rows are rescaled by 1/||x - m|| instead of 1/||x||, and the subset-mean centring inside spectrum_stats removes only a common shift, so the two spaces can give different values; with n samples it cannot exceed min(n - 1, dim), and bounded_by_samples marks the entries where n - 1 < dim for the clean subset or a flagged subsample",
    "prekey_rule": "for each encoder, the first seed's split of its main isotropy config (isotropy_<corpus>_<encoder>.yaml): make_split with the config's n_dev, n_tgt and min_tgt_images, as SeedContext of ijiss_btp.experiments.isotropy builds it; the mean of the split's DEV rows is subtracted from every embedding and each row is L2-normalised (center_normalize), which gives the experiments' pre-key embeddings; every statistic is then computed on the same fingers, images, pairs and seeds as in the raw space",
    "range_percentiles": [
